//// The library's enum. `Text` and `Bg` are SECTIONS: each desugars into an
//// inner enum (`__Token__Text`, `__Token__Text__Size`) that no module
//// exports, so every module that names one emits its own copy of its
//// classes — the consumer's `main`, this module, and `styler` all have
//// three different `__Token__Text__Size$X3xl` classes.
////
//// `X3xl` is unique in the program; `Lg` is declared twice (`Text.Size.Lg`
//// and `Bg.Lg`). That pair is the whole point of the cell: the two arms
//// took different lowerings on commonJS, and only the unique one was wrong.

pub type Token {
    Text {
        Bold,
        Size {
            Lg,
            X3xl,
        }
    }
    Bg {
        Lg,
    }
}
